* Food for the hungry corners (openc2e Creatures 2 project, our own script
* and our own art). Ideas from JayD's "Plato Project" (Creatures 2 COB):
* a bush whose fruit follows the season (his Cornucopia Bush) and hidden
* patches that keep regrowing the game's berries; none of his files are
* used. Sprites zfbs (the bush, one picture per season) and zfrt (four
* fruits, each bud, half-grown, ripe, overripe, then ripe and overripe
* lying on the ground) are drawn by art/fruitbush.py (the bush in four looks: zfbs, zfbm,
* zfbv, zfbw), and its sea look (zfbk, a kelp clump) and sea fruits
* (zfrk) by art/seaplant.py.
* Run by openc2e after the world loads (Additions folder); everything here
* is made anew each load, so the script is safe to repeat.

* The seasonal fruit bush (2 4 141). It is kept between sessions (OV99 =
* 7461 asks openc2e's world save to keep it). OV00 is its stage (0 seedling,
* 1 young, 2 full) and OV01 its age in 25-second steps: young after about
* 25 minutes, full after about an hour. Its picture is stage * 4 + season.
* Young bushes carry up to three fruits, full ones six, and a new bud comes
* every step while there is room (owner, 2026-11-16, "more food": Home's
* 150 creatures were starving at about 15 fruits a minute from 15 bushes;
* it was two and four, half the steps); a fruit grows on the
* bush from a green bud and drops when ripe. OV02 is the bush's look, made
* to suit where it grows (0 mossy green, sprite zfbs; 1 machine-cave teal
* and rust, zfbm; 2 volcanic ember-red, zfbv; 3 warm-rock bronze, zfbw; 4 desert sage,
* zfbd; 5 the sea, a kelp clump, zfbk, whose fruit are sea fruit, zfrk:
* sea grapes, kelp pod, sea plum, frost pearl);
* its fruit carries it, so a seedling takes its parent's look, except in
* the volcano (x 6400 on, below y 1780), where it is always volcanic, and
* under water, where it is always kelp (owner, 2026-11-11: a bush had
* seeded on the sea floor); a sea fruit that comes ashore grows a mossy
* bush.
* OV03 = 2 marks this version (full-grown 156 x 108). OV07 is its form: 0
* the full bush, 1 compact (108 x 80, zfc*, potted zfq*), 2 slender (56 x
* 118, zfn*, potted zfo*), for places too small for the full one (fruit
* places and how many it carries in the bud routine below).
* OV05 = 1: standing in a pot (a built floor, not earth).
scrp 2 4 141 9
  addv ov01 1
  doif ov00 eq 0
    doif ov01 ge 60 setv ov00 1 endi
  endi
  doif ov00 eq 1
    doif ov01 ge 150 setv ov00 2 endi
  endi
  setv var8 ov00 mulv var8 4 addv var8 sean pose var8
  * the soil (the nutrient cycle; owner, 2026-11-17: "modestly"): each
  * step the bush earns 75 to 125 growth (OV06) by the room's inorganic
  * nutrient (0 to 50 and up), and a bud for each 100, so bare soil grows
  * a quarter slower and rich soil a quarter faster; each bud draws one
  * unit of inorganic nutrient up. A potted bush (OV05 = 1, on decks and
  * ledges) grows in its pot's soil at the usual pace.
  setv var1 intr
  doif var1 gt 50 setv var1 50 endi
  doif var1 lt 0 setv var1 0 endi
  doif ov05 eq 1 setv var1 25 endi
  addv ov06 75 addv ov06 var1
  doif ov06 ge 100 subv ov06 100 gsub bud endi
  targ ownr
  doif ov06 ge 100 subv ov06 100 gsub bud endi
  stop
subr bud
  targ ownr
  * how many fruit it carries at once (OV07 is its form: 0 the full bush,
  * 1 compact, 2 slender): full 3 young and 6 grown, compact 2 and 4,
  * slender 1 and 3
  setv var9 ov00 mulv var9 3
  doif ov07 eq 1 setv var9 ov00 mulv var9 2 endi
  doif ov07 eq 2 setv var9 ov00 mulv var9 3 divv var9 2 endi
  setv var0 0
  esee 2 25 141 addv var0 1 next
  esee 2 25 142 addv var0 1 next
  esee 2 25 143 addv var0 1 next
  esee 2 25 144 addv var0 1 next
  doif var0 lt var9
    setv var1 0
    doif var1 eq 0
      * somewhere in the crown, over the leaves (measured on the pictures
      * of all four looks in every season: the crown is a dome, so the
      * height range depends on how far across; young bushes are smaller
      * and lower; the smaller forms below)
      setv var3 0 setv var5 0
      doif ov07 eq 0
        doif ov00 eq 2
          rndv var3 20 116
          doif var3 lt 40 rndv var5 47 55 endi
          doif var3 ge 40
            doif var3 lt 52 rndv var5 36 54 endi
          endi
          doif var3 ge 52
            doif var3 lt 88 rndv var5 29 56 endi
          endi
          doif var3 ge 88
            doif var3 lt 104 rndv var5 43 59 endi
          endi
          doif var3 ge 104 rndv var5 47 65 endi
        else
          rndv var3 68 76 rndv var5 52 72
        endi
      endi
      * the compact bush (108 x 80; measured the same way on all its looks
      * and seasons, plain and potted alike: a pot hangs below the picture)
      doif ov07 eq 1
        doif ov00 eq 2
          rndv var3 11 76
          doif var3 lt 23 rndv var5 30 39 endi
          doif var3 ge 23
            doif var3 lt 35 rndv var5 26 39 endi
          endi
          doif var3 ge 35
            doif var3 lt 59 rndv var5 21 40 endi
          endi
          doif var3 ge 59
            doif var3 lt 71 rndv var5 30 40 endi
          endi
          doif var3 ge 71 rndv var5 33 44 endi
        else
          rndv var3 38 50 rndv var5 34 50
        endi
      endi
      * the slender bush (56 x 118): a narrow crown up its top half
      doif ov07 eq 2
        doif ov00 eq 2
          rndv var3 5 24
          doif var3 lt 13 rndv var5 8 40 endi
          doif var3 ge 13
            doif var3 lt 17 rndv var5 6 56 endi
          endi
          doif var3 ge 17 rndv var5 6 24 endi
        else
          rndv var3 17 20 rndv var5 78 90
        endi
      endi
      setv var2 posl addv var2 var3
      setv var4 post addv var4 var5
      setv var6 sean mulv var6 6
      setv var7 sean addv var7 141
      setv var9 ov02
      * fruit draw just in front of their bush (OV04 is the bush's plane;
      * 1400 for a bush from before planes were kept)
      setv var8 1400
      doif ov04 ne 0 setv var8 ov04 addv var8 1 endi
      inst
      doif var9 eq 5
        new: simp zfrk 6 var6 var8 0
      else
        new: simp zfrt 6 var6 var8 0
      endi
      setv cls2 2 25 var7
      setv attr 0
      bhvr 0 0
      setv ov02 var9
      mvto var2 var4
      tick 600
      slow
      targ ownr
      doif ov05 ne 1
        doif intr gt 0 subv intr 1 endi
      endi
    endi
  endi
  retn
endm

* A fruit's life (pictures: 0 bud, 1 half-grown, 2 ripe, 3 overripe; 4
* and 5 are ripe and overripe lying on the ground, see event 6 below):
* it swells on the bush, drops when ripe, goes overripe on the ground, and
* rots (2 25 149, below); now and then a rotted fruit sprouts a seedling bush
* where it lay, if no bush stands within 200 px and there are fewer than 36 (16
* until 2026-11-16, when all 15 left no room to spread).
scrp 2 25 141 9
  doif pose eq 0
    pose 1 tick 600
  else
    doif pose eq 1
      * ripe: it drops, and creatures may eat it
      pose 2 setv attr 195 bhvr 0 64 setv accg 3 setv rest 30 setv grav 1 tick 6000
    else
      * overripe, lying as it was (2 ripe -> 3; 4 ripe on the ground -> 5)
      setv var9 0
      doif pose eq 2 pose 3 tick 3000 setv var9 1 endi
      doif pose eq 4 pose 5 tick 3000 setv var9 1 endi
      doif var9 eq 0
        * rotten: another object takes its place (the new picture's bottom
        * where the old one's was)
        setv var1 0
        doif ov02 eq 5 addv var1 4 endi
        mulv var1 2
        setv var2 posl setv var3 post setv var4 ov02
        inst new: simp zfrr 2 var1 1400 0
        setv cls2 2 25 149
        setv attr 195 bhvr 0 64
        setv accg 3 setv rest 30
        setv ov00 141 setv ov03 var4 setv ov01 0
        mvto var2 var3 setv grav 1
        tick 900
        slow
        kill ownr
      endi
    endi
  endi
endm
